submission_format:
Return a JSON object with the same keys and nesting as the example below.

```json
{
  "artifacts": {
    "calculation_log": "/workspace/output/calculations.json"
  },
  "results": {
    "fit": {
      "isotropic": 0.0,
      "uniaxial": 0.0
    }
  }
}
```

Units: fit.isotropic and fit.uniaxial in eV per unit strain.

Use the format below for the file `/workspace/output/calculations.json`:
JSON, one calculation per prescribed strain pair. Strains are dimensionless; cell/positions are Angstrom, masses are amu and the six signed mode energies are eV. The method field is optional descriptive metadata; the scorer identifies the numerical data from its fields, regardless of the method label.
```text
{"model":"teacher.model","dispersion":false,"default_dtype":"float64","calculations":[{"isotropic_strain":0.0,"uniaxial_strain":0.0,"structure":{"numbers":[14,14],"pbc":[true,true,true],"cell":[[0,2.715,2.715],[2.715,0,2.715],[2.715,2.715,0]],"positions":[[0,0,0],[1.3575,1.3575,1.3575]],"masses":[28.0855,28.0855]},"mode_energies_eV":[0,0,0,0.06,0.06,0.06]}]}
```
